- 2000 threads alive at once;
- recursion 1M deep on a thread;
- 80 lines of 70,000 characters from 4 threads, all whole;
- output order around joins;
- a failure on a nested thread, reported once with exit 22;
- a failure inside a locked statement releases the lock;
- a thread spawned and joined inside a locked method (the join lets go of the lock);
- stop() before start, after finish, and nested;
- read-only sharing of objects and files;
- copy-on-write lists passed to 4 threads while main appends;
- two threads writing different fields of one object;
- the checker reaching capsules used only through thread.new (S201, S210, S110 before anything runs).

Seen and not filed:
- stop() on a thread blocked inside join() does not end it. That fits 'stops between statements'.
- With 4 unjoined failures only the first report prints.
- An S724 notice can print after a fatal report.

Gaps in the documentation:
- There is no satellite.help topic for threads or .lock(), so help text could not be checked.
- THREADS.md's T1 table still says a second join of an object answer is S727. T2 and tests/threads_answer_object.satl share it, and satl shares it.
- The S721–S728 thread codes are not in SATELLITE_ERROR.md, where S0721–S0728 are config codes with look-alike numbers.

